Subject: «Apply» on KDE works even before the first display

A defect fix, not a feature. On KDE the wallpaper is shown by the waywallen
Plasma plugin, and the daemon gets a display only once the plugin is assigned
as the desktop wallpaper. Rexon assigns it itself, on pressing «Apply»
(previously — when the tab opened, and with an empty library the desktop went
black). The vendor «Apply» button is enabled by `hasSelection`, and that
needs at least one display: on a fresh system the circle closed, and the
button stayed grey forever (VM Arch + Plasma 6.8.2, 30.10.2026).

* `WallpaperDetailPanel.qml`: with zero targets the button is available if
  `W.App.applyWithoutDisplays` — the target is «all desktops» (empty
  `wireTargets`). The Rexon transport holds the frame until plasmashell
  registers a display; the decision is the core's
  (`waywallen_kde_plugin::apply_without_displays`, the same `apply_gate` as
  the transport's).
* `KdeDisplaysHelp.qml`: with zero displays, instead of «install the
  extension from GitHub/KDE Store and select it in the desktop settings» —
  the Rexon hint `W.App.noDisplaysHint` («choose a wallpaper and press
  „Apply“»). An empty string — the upstream look. On X11 outside KDE (MATE,
  XFCE, Cinnamon X11) the output is brought up by the Rexon host, and the
  hint is visible with any daemon backend (before that, under «No monitors
  registered» it was empty, 30.10.2026).

Playlists (`PlaylistListSheetState`) are separate, patch 0011: there targets
are chosen one by one, and with an empty list `every()` over the selected
displays would give «already playing».
---
diff --git a/ui/qml/component/KdeDisplaysHelp.qml b/ui/qml/component/KdeDisplaysHelp.qml
